WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
- Before he gave the vision,
he already made provisions

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.700
'cause he knew you guys
would wind up together.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.250
Even before you were formed
in your mother's womb,

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.910
he knew you.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.610
I just, I'm thankful.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.777
Oh, come here Antoni.

00:00:15.616 --> 00:00:16.756
Antoni.

00:00:16.756 --> 00:00:20.112
(group laughing)

00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:21.580
Oh, my baby.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.527
- Can I read a letter that I wrote to him?

00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:24.676
- Yes.

00:00:24.676 --> 00:00:25.552
- Okay. All right.

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:26.385
- Love to.

00:00:27.301 --> 00:00:29.395
(sighs)

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.840
(solemn piano music)

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.690
- Okay.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:33.573
Dear Dad,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.750
It hasn't rained in a week,

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.400
but as I reflect on you

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.420
the sky has suddenly opened

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.820
and poured out everything
it can no longer hold.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.280
Yesterday, and countless other days,

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.480
I am overwhelmed by emotion,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.693
and it too pours out.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.870
Through it all, I know

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.920
you would want me to live my fullest life,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.870
carrying on your name and legacy

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.313
even further than you did.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.020
And if what people say is true,

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.740
our loved ones really do
look down on us from heaven,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.520
then you already know
that I'm well on my way

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.253
being what you wanted me.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.423
If what people say is true,

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.960
then you also know that I am gay.

00:01:24.592 --> 00:01:26.940
(soft orchestral music)

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.940
These three words have been
an enormous wall between us.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.363
I'm sorry for not tearing
down the wall sooner.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.070
You were an incredible dad

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.873
and didn't deserve to be left out.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.493
Love, your son.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.263
So,

00:01:52.741 --> 00:01:55.510
I thought it was important to tell you

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.810
my truth,

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.063
that I'm gay.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:06.367
(sniffles)

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:09.920
I wish I could share this moment with Dad

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.710
and see how happy

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.713
happy I am.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.453
And-

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.055
(crying)

00:02:22.427 --> 00:02:23.712
- I'm happy for you

00:02:23.712 --> 00:02:28.712
♪ I can't do this alone. ♪

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.577
♪ Alone. ♪

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.708
- I'm sorry for keeping it from you.

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:42.875
- That's fine.

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:48.099
♪ Alone, alone. ♪

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:53.099
♪ Show me where I belong. ♪

00:02:57.148 --> 00:02:57.981
♪ Belong. ♪

00:02:57.981 --> 00:03:01.564
- But, the past 6 to 9 years they've been-

00:03:02.563 --> 00:03:04.233
it's been a trying time for me.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.297
I've dealt with so much stuff
that I can't talk about.

00:03:10.376 --> 00:03:12.698
I just hid it from you.

00:03:12.698 --> 00:03:14.865
(sobbing)

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.520
I don't think I would be here today

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.500
if I didn't have some of the people,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.143
some of the friends, some family like you.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.743
Not being honest,

00:03:41.962 --> 00:03:44.280
I mean I can't be just like,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.270
I dunno, it just felt like a lot.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.320
I don't have much family here.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.960
And you are my family

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.250
and I don't wanna lose you.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.800
- No, you won't.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.740
I'm always gonna be there for you.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.573
- You will?

00:03:56.573 --> 00:03:58.460
- Just like I know you gonna be for me.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.644
- Yes.

00:03:59.644 --> 00:04:00.477
(sighs)

00:04:00.477 --> 00:04:01.803
Okay, I'm relieved.

00:04:01.803 --> 00:04:04.053
(laughing)

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.400
Thank you.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.010
- For the first couple
days you kept saying

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.680
you can't fix ugly.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.390
And, it broke my heart.
- You all have fixed ugly.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.223
(laughs)

00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:14.900
- We have fallen in love with you.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.210
And I didn't really expect
to have this moment with you.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.103
And you are such an amazing man.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:23.658
- You guys are making me cry.

00:04:23.658 --> 00:04:24.491
(crying)

00:04:24.491 --> 00:04:25.324
- [Karamo] No, it's okay.

00:04:25.324 --> 00:04:26.730
- [Tan] Oh, we love you Thom.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.161
You're such a good man.

00:04:28.161 --> 00:04:31.578
(emotional guitar music)

00:04:38.476 --> 00:04:39.309
- I'm sorry.

00:04:39.309 --> 00:04:40.142
- [Karamo] No.
- [Tan] No.

00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:41.260
- We'll miss all of you guys.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.093
Cheers.

00:04:42.093 --> 00:04:42.980
- [Antoni] Cheers.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:43.860
- No more hiding.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.170
You ready to see?

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.620
Let's look at your new smile.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.765
(emotional guitar music)

00:04:53.765 --> 00:04:55.700
(crying)

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.694
- Thank you.

00:04:56.694 --> 00:04:58.295
(group laughing)

00:04:58.295 --> 00:05:00.462
(sobbing)

00:05:14.957 --> 00:05:16.058
I can smile again.

00:05:16.058 --> 00:05:17.141
- [Tan] Yeah.

00:05:21.381 --> 00:05:22.420
- Thank you.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.370
- It's my pleasure.

00:05:28.409 --> 00:05:31.560
(crowd cheering)

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.643
(crying)

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.783
- Everything in my life
has brought me to you.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.253
All my regrets,

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.320
all my choices,

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.680
all my tears.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.100
I wouldn't change a thing.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.620
I'm ready for our next step to begin.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.073
I'm ready for us.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.103
Shannon Anne Eller,

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.040
will you marry me?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:05:59.958
Be my wife?

00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:00.791
- Yes.

00:06:00.791 --> 00:06:03.458
(crow cheering)

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.340
- This got me.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:12.173
- I know.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.794
How was it when he first
told you he was gay?

00:06:16.794 --> 00:06:18.370
He told you when he was 14, right?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.260
- Around 14.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.417
It took me aback, you know,

00:06:20.417 --> 00:06:22.443
for a minute, and for a while.

00:06:22.443 --> 00:06:24.480
And it was a process.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.290
Brenda, she was one that was always

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.000
you know, she would talk to me

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.410
you know, about it.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.190
When God enlightened my heart,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.383
we sat around this very table, I sat here,

00:06:34.383 --> 00:06:35.996
he sat there.

00:06:35.996 --> 00:06:39.451
And I said, "Mama needs
to apologize to you."

00:06:39.451 --> 00:06:42.227
And he looked at me in
the eyes and he was like,

00:06:42.227 --> 00:06:43.287
"For what Mama?"

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.440
I said, "Because

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:47.970
Mama

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:48.803
loves you,

00:06:48.803 --> 00:06:50.010
you know that right?"

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.520
And he said, "Yes."

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.010
I said, "But I need to
ask you your forgiveness.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.567
Because Mama has not loved
you unconditionally."

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.317
And, you know, he looked at me,

00:07:03.317 --> 00:07:05.978
"Mama, I forgave you a long time ago."

00:07:05.978 --> 00:07:10.226
And I said, "No, I need
to hear you say that."

00:07:10.226 --> 00:07:14.360
I said, "Because, the Bible
that I reads tell me that if

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:17.995
I have wronged somebody,
or mistreated someone,

00:07:17.995 --> 00:07:20.720
to ask their forgiveness first.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.440
And then I'm free to go to the Father."

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.273
- [Tan] Yes.

00:07:23.273 --> 00:07:24.937
- And I told him at that point,

00:07:24.937 --> 00:07:27.360
"Your Mama has your back."
- Yeah.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.580
- She thought her faith told her

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.950
to judge somebody who was gay.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.820
But she chose to see past that

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.050
and she saw the individual,

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.490
she saw the person that her son is,

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.660
and she changed her mind.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.330
She says that it was a
religious experience,

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.063
but she made that choice.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.046
Not all parents do that.

00:07:45.046 --> 00:07:47.963
(machines beeping)

00:07:50.211 --> 00:07:54.044
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.500
- [Karamo] This is his top surgery.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.970
- And when we say top surgery

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.480
we mean to get rid of the breasts?

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.313
- Yes.

00:08:09.313 --> 00:08:11.383
(whistles)

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:19.450
- [Man Voiceover] I was born
and identified as a woman.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.476
But since I was in preschool,

00:08:21.476 --> 00:08:24.510
I've known that that just wasn't me.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:27.320
I remember when I was 12 years
old standing in a mirror,

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.850
and contorting my body in different ways

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.870
to be seen as more masculine.
- [Tan] Whoa.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.670
Thinking, I'm gonna get a surgery

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.770
that makes my body look like this one day.

00:08:37.689 --> 00:08:39.524
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:08:39.524 --> 00:08:42.441
(machines beeping)

00:08:46.382 --> 00:08:48.715
(murmuring)

00:08:49.906 --> 00:08:51.280
- We finished your surgery.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.490
- Wanna take a little quick peek?

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.893
(emotional piano music)

00:09:02.022 --> 00:09:02.855
- Oh!

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.063
- [Antoni] He just looked
down for the first time.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.462
(machines beeping)

00:09:11.462 --> 00:09:13.712
(laughing)

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:16.460
- Wow.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.090
- We all struggled with coming
to the realization of that

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.950
we were different than everyone else.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.780
And I can only imagine
just how hard it was

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.390
to realize that you weren't
born with the right body.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.200
That he was able to come
to that realization,

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.250
and take the steps to
become who he truly is.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.283
He's an inspiration.

00:09:33.835 --> 00:09:36.910
- I'm blown away by how
fearlessly you embraced

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:37.743
this transformation.

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:38.576
- Right.

00:09:38.576 --> 00:09:39.409
(laughing)

00:09:39.409 --> 00:09:40.242
Exactly.

00:09:40.242 --> 00:09:41.100
Like, I feel like radiant,

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.540
and beautiful, and sexy,
- You are.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.140
and confident.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.550
I had it in me, but
you all brought it out,

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.765
and I really appreciate it.

00:09:48.765 --> 00:09:50.570
(guitar music)

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.740
I just feel like

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:58.350
I had pretty much given up
on kind, genuine people.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.400
Like really, I did.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.870
Because everyone that I met,

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.000
I felt like they pitied me,
and they looked down on me,

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.640
and, you know, they expected
me to be someone else,

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.300
more black, less white,
more gay, less gay.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.990
I'd basically just accepted
that the real world sucks,

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:18.360
and family doesn't exist,
unconditional love doesn't exist.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:21.110
But you all just showed me
that it's beautiful and sexy

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.348
to like care for yourself.

00:10:22.348 --> 00:10:23.181
- Yeah.

00:10:23.181 --> 00:10:24.014
- You know what I mean?

00:10:24.014 --> 00:10:27.640
And it's like, cute and
confident to just be black,

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.140
and be gay, and be a woman,

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.443
and what that is is me, I'm always that.

00:10:31.443 --> 00:10:32.760
- Yes.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.542
- So, when we were
packing up the old house,

00:10:36.542 --> 00:10:37.375
- Okay.

00:10:37.375 --> 00:10:38.800
- you know, I told you
I wanted to make sure

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:42.965
I made a very special place
for you to keep your memories.

00:10:42.965 --> 00:10:44.320
- Oh, man.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:46.924
- And all the cards said, you know,

00:10:46.924 --> 00:10:49.130
"Be nice to your brother."
- "Be nice to your brother."

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:50.740
- So what I did was

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.640
- Oh my goodness.

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:54.233
- I had it made in her handwriting.

00:10:56.826 --> 00:10:57.740
(laughs)

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.053
- Oh, that's beautiful.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:00.903
Oh my goodness.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.130
That is amazing.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.950
(emotional piano music)

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:08.020
Thank you so much.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.400
That's beautiful.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.460
- I thank god for this week.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:14.630
This week we worked with the Fab Five.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:15.830
They put their whole heart

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.743
into the community center out there.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.360
These are five gifted men

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.550
who are gay.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.440
And through the course of the week,

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.760
you know, we were able to
build some relationships.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:32.373
That's what it's about,
building relationships.

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:36.970
They shared with me
how they have been just

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.513
torn down and rejected.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:44.750
And the church has turned
their backs on them.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:47.950
How can I say that I love God,

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:52.558
but I cannot love the ones that
are right there next to me?

00:11:52.558 --> 00:11:53.800
(clapping)

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.560
I would call myself a hypocrite.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:12:00.500
And I say I was around five gay men,

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.813
I was around six.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.010
My son walked away from the church

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:08.110
you know, and it's been my prayer

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:11.040
that he comes here and feel the love

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:16.030
you know, the love that Pastor
Fava founded this place on.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:19.380
The love that surrounds me every Sunday.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.725
Do I love Jesus?

00:12:20.725 --> 00:12:22.380
Yes.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.990
Am I a believer?

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.590
Yes.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.830
Do I love my son?

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.216
Yes.

00:12:29.216 --> 00:12:30.144
Yes.

00:12:30.144 --> 00:12:30.977
(clapping)

00:12:30.977 --> 00:12:31.950
Yes.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:32.783
Yes.

